# Tasks: SUBTASK-STATE-MACHINE

Spec: SubtaskStateMachine

Purpose:
  Define the unit-level execution lifecycle for SUBTASK — the
  smallest execution unit in the MODUL -> CASE -> TASK -> SUBTASK
  hierarchy (bax ../branches/DOWN-UP-TRANSITION.sdd). A subtask is
  executed by exactly one /sdd-next --subtask resolution; every gate
  transition below is MANDATORY — security is a state-machine
  transition, not a checklist.

Owns:
  Subtask lifecycle states
  Subtask state transitions
  Subtask failure/rework loops
  Unit-level progress recording

States:

  TODO            — Unit defined, not yet started
  IN_PROGRESS     — Implementation in progress (single unit scope)
  IMPLEMENTED     — Code/artifact produced, ready for review
  CR_REVIEW       — Code review of the unit in progress
  REFACTORED      — CR findings addressed (or CR passed clean)
  SECURITY_REVIEW — Scoped security validation of the unit
  TESTING         — Unit-level validation running
  PASSED          — All unit gates green
  DONE            — Unit closed with done-proof recorded
  REWORK          — Remediation in progress after a failed gate
  BLOCKED         — Cannot proceed: explicit blocker declared

MainFlow:

  TODO -> IN_PROGRESS -> IMPLEMENTED -> CR_REVIEW -> REFACTORED ->
  SECURITY_REVIEW -> TESTING -> PASSED -> DONE

ReworkLoops:

  CR review failure:
    CR_REVIEW -> REWORK -> CR_REVIEW
    (re-implement within unit scope, then re-review)

  Security failure:
    SECURITY_REVIEW -> REWORK -> SECURITY_REVIEW
    (security findings fixed within unit scope, re-validated)

  Test failure:
    TESTING -> REWORK -> TESTING
    (defect fixed within unit scope, re-tested)

  Blocked:
    ANY_STATE -> BLOCKED  (requires explicit blocker declaration)
    BLOCKED -> previous_state  (when blocker resolved)

TransitionRules:

  [ST1] DONE is reachable ONLY via PASSED — never a direct
        TODO -> DONE transition, and never from a gate state that
        has not reported green.
  [ST2] The next subtask is resolvable only when the current unit is
        DONE (No DONE -> No Next Unit — bax EXECUTION-CONTRACT.sdd
        CoreInvariants).
  [ST3] Gate order is fixed: no SECURITY_REVIEW before CR_REVIEW has
        passed on the same unit revision; no TESTING before
        SECURITY_REVIEW passed (security precedes test, v2 ordering
        — mirrors chains/delivery.sdd branch sub-path).
  [ST4] Every rework loop iteration MUST record progress
        (BEFORE/CHANGE/AFTER/RESULT) and is capped by LOOP-PROTECTION
        guards — repetition without progress escalates to BLOCKED.
  [ST5] REWORK stays INSIDE unit scope: allowed paths/actions come
        from the subtask schema; anything beyond scope is a new
        subtask or a task-level change, never a silent expansion.
  [ST6] BLOCKED and DONE are the only terminal exits; BLOCKED
        resolution returns to the state that declared it.

ProgressRule:

  Each gate transition and each rework iteration MUST record:
    BEFORE:    measurable state before the action
    CHANGE:    what was changed
    AFTER:     measurable state after the action
    RESULT:    outcome (pass/fail/blocked)

Mapping (unit lifecycle -> delivery chain):

  CR_REVIEW        -> CR (scoped instance)
  REFACTORED       -> RF (scoped instance, conditional)
  SECURITY_REVIEW  -> SC (scoped instance)
  TESTING          -> XX-TS (scoped instance)
  PASSED           -> all scoped gates green for the unit

  Subtasks that span multiple layers inherit the DL1 v2 branch
  sub-path ordering per layer (CR -> RF -> SC -> TS, bax
  ../chains/delivery.sdd).

Navigation:
  TaskStateMachine: @TASK-STATE-MACHINE.sdd
  SubtaskSchema: @../schemas/subtask.sdd
  ExecutionContract: @EXECUTION-CONTRACT.sdd
  LoopProtection: @LOOP-PROTECTION.sdd
  DoneProof: @DONE-PROOF.sdd
  DownUpTransition: @../branches/DOWN-UP-TRANSITION.sdd
  DeliveryChain: @../chains/delivery.sdd
  NextCommand: @../commands/sdd-next.sdd

State: +
  (Phase 155: created as the unit-level lifecycle backing
   /sdd-next --subtask resolution; states mirror TASK-STATE-MACHINE
   discipline at unit granularity; [ST3] encodes the v2
   security-before-test ordering)
